# A hand-written bicubic Bézier cap — the general-NURBS-patch fixture surface
# (DECISIONS.md "the general NURBS patch…", slice 1). Single-span clamped knots
# make the patch pure Bézier, so its anchors are hand-derivable: the centre is
# the pole average with weights (1,3,3,1)/8 per direction — apex at
# (12, 12, 4·(3·3·16)/64 = 9.0) with a vertical normal — and every boundary
# pole sits at z = 0, so the four boundary curves (and the surface minimum)
# lie exactly in z = 0. Poles are row-major (n_u rows of n_v poles), mm by
# definition; the NurbsPatch feature's x/y/z place the sheet in stock coords.
degree_u 3
degree_v 3
knots_u 0 0 0 0 1 1 1 1
knots_v 0 0 0 0 1 1 1 1
pole 0 0 0
pole 0 8 0
pole 0 16 0
pole 0 24 0
pole 8 0 0
pole 8 8 16
pole 8 16 16
pole 8 24 0
pole 16 0 0
pole 16 8 16
pole 16 16 16
pole 16 24 0
pole 24 0 0
pole 24 8 0
pole 24 16 0
pole 24 24 0
